    title: "From arson to land seizures: Settlers tighten grip on Palestinian villages near Ramallah",
    summary: "From arson to land seizures: Settlers tighten grip on Palestinian villages near Ramallah In a series of coordinated attacks across several villages near the city of Ramallah in the central occupied West Bank, Israeli settlers torched Palestinian vehicles between Saturday evening and Sunday morning. The settlers also spray-painted racist slogans on the walls of homes in the three villages, calling for the killing of Arabs and for revenge against them. Rafat Abu Musa, head of the village council of Deir al-Sudan, north of Ramallah, told Middle East Eye that settlers infiltrated the southern part of the village at 11.30pm on Saturday and burned down two vehicles. They spray-painted slogans in Hebrew on the walls of nearby houses, he said, adding that the same area had been targeted by a similar attack two months ago, during which a vehicle was set on fire. Abu Musa indicated that the settlers came from a newly built outpost on the summit of Jabal al-Ras, located in the neighbouring village of Umm Safa. h",
    preview: "From arson to land seizures: Settlers tighten grip on Palestinian villages near Ramallah In a series of coordinated attacks across several villages near the city of Ramallah in the central occupied West Bank, Israeli settlers torched Palestinian vehicles between Saturday evening and Sunday morning. The settlers also spray-painted racist slogans on the walls of homes in the three villages, calling for the killing of Arabs and for revenge against them.",
    body: "From arson to land seizures: Settlers tighten grip on Palestinian villages near Ramallah In a series of coordinated attacks across several villages near the city of Ramallah in the central occupied West Bank, Israeli settlers torched Palestinian vehicles between Saturday evening and Sunday morning. The settlers also spray-painted racist slogans on the walls of homes in the three villages, calling for the killing of Arabs and for revenge against them.\n\nRafat Abu Musa, head of the village council of Deir al-Sudan, north of Ramallah, told Middle East Eye that settlers infiltrated the southern part of the village at 11.30pm on Saturday and burned down two vehicles. They spray-painted slogans in Hebrew on the walls of nearby houses, he said, adding that the same area had been targeted by a similar attack two months ago, during which a vehicle was set on fire.\n\nAbu Musa indicated that the settlers came from a newly built outpost on the summit of Jabal al-Ras, located in the neighbouring village of Umm Safa. h",
