    title: "Israel carries out more demolitions in southern Lebanon",
    summary: "Israel carries out more demolitions in southern Lebanon Israeli forces detonated explosives to destroy structures on the outskirts of Qantara in southern Lebanon , Lebanon's National News Agency (NNA) reported. Earlier on Sunday, Israeli forces set off a massive explosion in Zawtar al-Sharqiyah, followed by another in Kfar Tibnit, according to NNA. The blasts could be heard across much of southern Lebanon. Residents of Nabatieh al-Fawqa and Zawtar held two separate protests against the Lebanese government's \"silence\" over Israel's occupation of areas up to the Litani River, which began in March, according to NNA. Parliament Speaker Nabih Berri said he would not accept congratulations on Lebanon's Independence Day, which falls on 22 November, in solidarity with residents of the occupied southern border villages. In a statement, Berri described this year's independence as \"incomplete and unfulfilled\". He said it would be complete only once Lebanese territory was liberated and official and popular positions were united again.",
    preview: "Israel carries out more demolitions in southern Lebanon Israeli forces detonated explosives to destroy structures on the outskirts of Qantara in southern Lebanon , Lebanon's National News Agency (NNA) reported. Earlier on Sunday, Israeli forces set off a massive explosion in Zawtar al-Sharqiyah, followed by another in Kfar Tibnit, according to NNA. The blasts could be heard across much of southern Lebanon.",
    body: "Israel carries out more demolitions in southern Lebanon Israeli forces detonated explosives to destroy structures on the outskirts of Qantara in southern Lebanon , Lebanon's National News Agency (NNA) reported. Earlier on Sunday, Israeli forces set off a massive explosion in Zawtar al-Sharqiyah, followed by another in Kfar Tibnit, according to NNA. The blasts could be heard across much of southern Lebanon.\n\nResidents of Nabatieh al-Fawqa and Zawtar held two separate protests against the Lebanese government's \"silence\" over Israel's occupation of areas up to the Litani River, which began in March, according to NNA. Parliament Speaker Nabih Berri said he would not accept congratulations on Lebanon's Independence Day, which falls on 22 November, in solidarity with residents of the occupied southern border villages.\n\nIn a statement, Berri described this year's independence as \"incomplete and unfulfilled\". He said it would be complete only once Lebanese territory was liberated and official and popular positions were united again.",
